Z||000024||batboy||07-13-99||08:36 PM||||I don't know much about turbocharging V6's, but on a Chevy small block V8, it's highly recommended to use low-compression, dished, forged pistons. Same with supercharging engines, must use low-compression, forged pistons.
Z||000025||lowCG||07-13-99||10:26 PM||||Yeah,I'd be a little nervous with stock pistons,after some experience with failing,lower quality pistons,but around 9:1 works great,any less and the car is a dog off the line,no fun to drive(okay,most cars,I'm not talking about F1 cars or anything).
